{"discussion":"Found the bug. In totals.py, apply() computes destination = bucket(change.after) once and uses it for ALL contributions. But a correction can change depot/item, so the 'before' receipt (negative units) belongs to a DIFFERENT bucket than the 'after' receipt (positive units). The fix: compute destination per-receipt inside the loop.","account":"Task: stock report shows incorrect quantities after corrections. Bug found in totals.py: apply() uses bucket(change.after) as destination for all contributions, but a correction changing depot/item means the old (negative) contribution should target the OLD bucket, not the new one. Fix: move destination = bucket(receipt) inside the for loop. entries.py is correct. Need to patch totals.py, run check public, submit.","operation":{"action":"patch","path":"src/dispatchledger/reporting/totals.py","old":"    def apply(self, change: Change) -> None:
        destination = bucket(change.after)
        for receipt, units in contributions(change):
            self._units[destination] = self._units.get(destination, 0) + units
            if self._units[destination] == 0:
                del self._units[destination]","new":"    def apply(self, change: Change) -> None:
        for receipt, units in contributions(change):
            destination = bucket(receipt)
            self._units[destination] = self._units.get(destination, 0) + units
            if self._units[destination] == 0:
                del self._units[destination]","expected_candidate_id":"cb2c2d7e160c4c829b71ae1a033d34e1416224bfab84d57477857c94a731f349","expected_file_sha256":"e1bf5143cbc452f69ef8358c5ccf91dcf7537520e7780eb6c64611c8cca24072"}}
